The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
requestsToInvalidate.add(entity.getRequestId());
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `getRequestId()` method can return `null`, and when this happens, there is no fallback mechanism in place to retrieve the `requestId` from the associated `stageEntity`. As a result, the upgrade process is unable to proceed, getting stuck at a manual prompt due to unresolved status calculations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
Long requestId = entity.getRequestId();
if (requestId == null) {
    StageEntity stageEntity = entity.getStage();
    if (stageEntity != null) {
        requestId = stageEntity.getRequestId();
    }
}
requestsToInvalidate.add(requestId);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a fallback mechanism that checks if the `requestId` is `null`. If it is, the code attempts to retrieve the `requestId` from the associated `stageEntity`. This ensures that a valid `requestId` is always added to the `requestsToInvalidate` set, preventing the upgrade process from getting stuck due to missing information.

